{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Prevent a recurrence of the 2026-08-26 `/var/gerrit` disk-fill from investigation evidence\n\n## Why\nThe acute `/var/gerrit` disk-fill incident (`wakeful-ordinary-chicken` / `5a05`) was dominated by one-off investigation evidence written to the Gerrit data volume: `/var/gerrit/rebar-quiet-window-evidence/` held two `epoch-probe-20260826T*` dumps of about 5.2G each (~11G total, 65% of used space). They were reclaimed with operator approval on 2026-08-30, taking `/var/gerrit` from 37% to 15%. That was true when this ticket was filed, but current main now prevents silent recurrence: observability.sh publishes data_disk_debris_bytes for non-site/lost+found top-level /var/gerrit debris, Terraform defines the rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris alarm, and review-bot-ops.md points to the dedicated gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md runbook.\n\nThis is the carried-over `/var/gerrit` sibling for disk-ceiling epic `endowed-upset-scaup` (`6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`). It is linked to that epic with `relates_to` rather than as a blocking edge so the ADR/scratch/root-accumulator stories remain claimable; the epic acceptance criteria require this ticket to be resolved or explicitly dispositioned before epic close.\n\n## What\nAdd policy/guarding and runbook coverage so investigation/probe evidence does not accumulate on `/var/gerrit`. Establish the approved evidence/scratch location (prefer the new bounded gate scratch path once S1 lands, or another explicitly capped temporary location) and document how to reclaim `/var/gerrit` data-volume headroom safely.\n\n## Scope\nIn scope: `/var/gerrit` data-volume runbook, guard/policy for probe evidence paths, optional metric/check for non-`site/` debris, and local tests if code changes are required. Out of scope: root-volume Docker/journald/tmp/container caps and gate scratch EBS provisioning, which are tracked by sibling stories under `endowed-upset-scaup`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Investigation/probe output does not land on the Gerrit data volume (`/var/gerrit`) without an explicit, bounded, documented exception.\n- [x] A guard, check, or loud failure path prevents or flags probe output under `/var/gerrit` before it can silently accumulate.\n- [x] Probe artifacts are bounded at spawn or stored under a capped scratch location so they self-clean rather than accumulate.\n- [x] `infra/runbooks/review-bot-ops.md` documents `/var/gerrit` data-disk reclaim/headroom diagnosis and safe remediation, not only root-volume Docker prunes.\n- [x] Optional non-`site/` `/var/gerrit` debris metric/alarm is either implemented or explicitly rejected with rationale in the ticket/runbook.\n- [x] Portability criterion: any guard/check uses host-level scripts/runbooks and local validation, not a GitHub-only CI trigger.\n\n## Notes / scope boundary\nThe slower data-disk growth driver from tickets-branch enrichment fan-out/blob-inclusive store remains separate work tracked by `4520`/`536b`/`0754`; do not duplicate that here.\n\n## Closeout remediation (2026-09-10)\n\nPlan-review found the remaining plan text contradicted current main: the guard/check and runbook work already landed in Gerrit 2586 under related bug `3276-2f81-8c75-4ddd`, and the ticket's own 2026-09-03 assessment states the detection is live in production. This edit reconciles the premise with that fact rather than re-implementing already-landed detection. The original problem is addressed: investigation evidence has a documented non-/var/gerrit location, non-site /var/gerrit debris is measured by `data_disk_debris_bytes` and alarmed by `rebar-gerrit-data-disk-debris`, and review-bot-ops links operators to `infra/runbooks/gerrit-data-volume-reclaim.md`. The stronger capped-scratch-volume ambition belongs to related epic `6202-e1c7-c57f-4897`, not this closeout ticket.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1789042207285774001,"uuid":"d2fc0578-ef7e-4acc-aad4-dfa2d97cf57f"}